As last week, very few changes in the interest of not breaking save
compatibility and also in the interest of just letting it stay
relatively consistent for awhile.

The only significant change is with the hit dice; this should bring
critters such as locusts and dragons (MZ_TINY and MZ_GIGANTIC,
respectively) more in line with what could be expected of such monsters.

8/18:
All 'e' monsters now non-genocidable to be consistent with magical eyes
 (after all, they're basically magical constructs like golems)
TIMED_DELAY defined so that using non-teleport 'runmodes' will work properly
Typo fix: missing comma between two particular armor-shop strings

8/14:
Alert version for "Q" command changed to 0.2.0; suppress_alert:0.3.0 in .RC file will now work properly
Monsters' hit dice now based partly on their size; bigger monsters roll bigger dice, smaller ones roll smaller dice
Cosmetic: a couple more 'Nethack' references changed to 'SporkHack'

